  "last_message": "I implemented `can_cancel` in `larder/cancellation.py`, and both existing tests still pass.\n\nThe rule comes from `docs/features/cancellation.md`: a member can cancel a pantry order until 2 hours before its pickup slot starts, and not after. The function returns `now <= pickup_starts - timedelta(hours=CUTOFF_HOURS)`, with `CUTOFF_HOURS = 2`, the same way `sessions.py` keeps its expiry time in a constant.\n\n- **Exactly 2 hours before pickup:** I count that moment as still allowed, reading \"until\" as including the cutoff itself. If it should be blocked instead, change `<=` to `<`.\n- **No tests yet:** neither existing test touches cancellation, so \"passing\" here only means nothing else broke. I can add tests for just before, exactly at and just after the cutoff if you want.",
